    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, the musical thing helps. but how does it actually \"find\" the frequencies? like is there some kind of process that pulls the individual waves out of the messy signal? do they just sort of appear?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The transformation process works by correlating the original signal with every possible pure sine and cosine wave. It calculates how much of the messy signal matches each specific test frequency. If the signal contains a lot of a 5 Hz wave, the correlation with the 5 Hz test wave will yield a large value, essentially \"pulling out\" that frequency's contribution from the overall mix.",
      "source": "target",
