      "content": "Even with chaotic noise, the correlation technique still works, but the noise will appear as a large portion of energy spread across many frequencies. Purely random noise, statistically, is spread uniformly across the entire frequency spectrum, which is what we see in the transform. However, if the signal we are interested in is much stronger than the noise, the underlying patterns will still be visible above the noisy background.",
